<% content_for :preheader, "One click to hear from us when #{@feature_name} ships. Nothing happens until you do." %>

<h1 style="margin:0 0 16px; font-size:21px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-0.4px; line-height:1.2; color:#16150f;">
  Confirm your place on the list
</h1>

<%# Phrased as "this address was entered", never "you signed up": the person
    reading this may not be the person who typed it, and a form that anyone can
    submit does not get to tell somebody what they did. %>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px; color:#57564e;">
  This address was entered on Tastatur to hear about <strong style="color:#16150f;"><%= @feature_name %></strong>
  when it ships. Confirm below and we will email you once — when it is ready.
</p>

<%= render "devise/mailer/button", url: @confirm_url, label: "Confirm" %>

<p style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:1.6px; text-transform:uppercase; color:#8c8a80;">
  What we do with this
</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 20px; font-size:13px; color:#57564e;">
  We keep the address and nothing else — no name, no company, no tracking of whether
  you opened this. It is used for one email about <%= @feature_name %> and is not
  added to any other list. You can remove it at any time from the page the button
  above takes you to, and removing it deletes the address rather than marking it
  unsubscribed.
  <a href="<%= Tastatur.base_url %>/privacy" style="color:#00628f;">How we handle data</a>.
</p>

<%# The way off, for the case that matters most: somebody who did not do this.
    Ignoring the message is genuinely sufficient — an unconfirmed address is
    swept within a week and is never mailed again in the meantime. %>
<p style="margin:0; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid #e3e1d8; font-size:13px; color:#8c8a80;">
  If you did not enter this address, ignore this message. Nothing is on any list until
  the button above is clicked, and an address that is never confirmed is deleted within
  a week.
</p>
